  EnumDecl
    LineComment "// User-defined method calls fold at compile time: a method with a body is"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// evaluated with self bound to the receiver, exactly as a top-level function"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// call is. The folder reaches the method table without a type query — the"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// receiver's type comes either from the value (an enum constant carries its"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// definition) or syntactically from the declared annotation in scope (a nominal"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// type over a primitive: a conversion's type name, a constant's annotation, a"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// method's result), so methods fold in const initializers, asserts, and other"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// pure positions."
    Newline "\n"
